0..76 Comment "// The circle with one point and a loop at it. The loop is a free invertible"
77..155 Comment "// cell at the point, so the paths from the point to itself are the words over"
156..234 Comment "// the loop and its inverse, with the two cancellations as rules: the lowering"
235..308 Comment "// mints them, and `Path(Circle, Base, Base)` is that presented type. The"
309..386 Comment "// integers are presented the same way, so the winding number folds the words"
387..460 Comment "// into them and spinning folds them back, each fold respecting the other"
461..491 Comment "// side\'s rules by conversion."
493..566 Comment "/// The circle: one point and a loop at it, bound as `loop : Path(Circle,"
567..584 Comment "/// Base, Base)`."
